  "doc": {
    "description": "init on a purely combinational gate (no feedback).\n\nThe output gate is a buffer (OR with both inputs tied to A), seeded to 1\nby the init block. With no feedback the seed is transient: at cycle 0 O\nreads the seeded 1, but the very first tick recomputes O := A OR A = A,\nso a poke of A=0 + one step yields 0 — the seed does not stick. Pins\nthat meta.init seeds the current buffer of an ordinary gate at power-on\nand that reset restores the seed (shdl.md §11.4; AMB-3 / AMB-39\npower-on state, witnessed at cycle 0 vs after a tick).",
